./logs/iter_004_ideas.stderr.log:1081:Failed completely for the problem's pseudo-regret. If a policy may depend on both the exogenous law \(P\) and the horizon \(T\), it can choose an \(\varepsilon_T\)-optimal fixed quote for \(V_T^P(a)=\mathbb E_P\sum_t r_t(a)\) and play it every round. This gives \(R_T^P\le\varepsilon_T=o(T)\) for every process, so no nontrivial tail condition can be necessary under this quantifier order. This failure relies on pseudo-regret, exogeneity, and horizon/law awareness.
./logs/iter_004_ideas.stderr.log:1089:Failed. Removing horizon awareness from the process-aware oracle regime is a real restriction. On the known deterministic path \(0^N,1/2,1\), the same early quotes must serve both prefixes \(N+1\) and \(N+2\), whose best fixed quotes approach \(1/2\) and \(1\), respectively. LB-011 shows one of the two prefix regrets is \(\Omega(N)\). Thus the horizon-aware collapse CL-014 does not automatically extend to one anytime policy.
