./logs/iter_011_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:2254:- Luo, Senapati, and Sharan (NeurIPS/OpenReview 2025) is verified. Its simultaneous-regret/calibration viewpoint is a loose analogy for simultaneous-prefix compatibility, not a delayed-feedback or market-making result.
./logs/iter_011_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:2255:- Hu, Tian, and Yang (COLT 2026/arXiv:2602.17577) is verified. It develops simultaneous Blackwell approachability with coupled actions for multiclass omniprediction; useful analogy for simultaneous-prefix feasibility, not direct support for the delayed market-making lower bounds.
