./logs/iter_011_synthesis.stderr.log:1804:Failed. Removing horizon awareness from the process-aware oracle regime is a real restriction. On the known deterministic path \(0^N,1/2,1\), the same early quotes must serve both prefixes \(N+1\) and \(N+2\), whose best fixed quotes approach \(1/2\) and \(1\), respectively. LB-011 shows one of the two prefix regrets is \(\Omega(N)\). Thus the horizon-aware collapse CL-014 does not automatically extend to one anytime policy.
