./logs/iter_011_synthesis.stderr.log:7050: Iteration 9 adds two internal results: the exact finite-\(C\) local root formula \(\kappa(C)=\delta_*(C)\), and the universal equal-revenue \(1/e\) upper bound for exogenous horizon-oblivious paths. A narrow literature check found robust/minimax-pricing analogies but no direct source for the exact root formula or the delayed-market-making \(1/e\) theorem. Treat Bergemann-Schlag 2011 and Caldentey-Liu-Lobel 2017 as adjacent context only, and Anagnostides et al. 2026 as a weak approachability analogy only.
./logs/iter_011_synthesis.stderr.log:7054:+Iteration 11 adds the compact suffix-menu local formula and the resulting path-aware known-path sufficient condition. The robust/minimax-pricing sources above remain adjacent analogies for randomized pricing, finite approximation, and LP/minimax structure; no external source found in the iteration reports proves the compact strict-crossing menu formula or the delayed-market-making suffix theorem. The alternating-path stress test confirms the suffix-menu condition is sufficient only.
./logs/iter_011_synthesis.stderr.log:7062: Iteration 10 leaves a cleaner checklist: write the monotone-threshold derandomization lemma with the grid/Hoeffding/Borel-Cantelli proof; optionally write the sharper bracketing \(O(n^{2/3})\) version if a precise monotone-entropy theorem is cited or proved; then state the deterministic-policy \(1/e\) theorem as a nonconstructive existence result. Do not present it as progress on the original iff.
