./logs/iter_011_synthesis.stderr.log:14187:+But the horizon-oblivious known-path policy \(a_t=1-\varepsilon_t\), with \(\frac1T\sum_{t\le T}\varepsilon_t\to0\), has \(o(T)\) regret. At even horizons it nearly matches the comparator \(1^-\) on all previous quotes. At odd horizons it loses only the same accumulated \(\varepsilon_t\)'s plus an \(O(1)\) boundary effect near the final \(1/2\). Thus the compact suffix-menu bound is sufficient only, not necessary.
